:::column 0.45
![Developer building things](https://github.com/abhisheknaiidu/abhisheknaiidu/blob/master/code.gif?raw=true)
:::
:::

I build things **from scratch** to understand how they really work: memory allocators, a POSIX-style shell, a ray tracer, a Linux system compiled from source.

42's model has no lectures and no teachers. Every project is defended in front of peers, so you either understand it or you fail. That shaped how I write code: **readable, leak-free, defensible.**

**Currently**

- 🛰️ Leading work on **ft_transcendence**, a 5-person real-time web app
- 🧱 Building **mini-baas**, a Backend-as-a-Service, outside the curriculum
- 🔍 Looking for **internships / junior roles** in systems or backend

